# Deterministic line endings.
#
# Without this, whether a file arrives in a commit as LF or CRLF depends on each
# contributor's core.autocrlf setting. That is how pull request #21 came to
# rewrite all 5,864 lines of InstanceTree.jrag while changing nothing: the diff
# was CRLF-versus-LF, not code.
#
# Deliberately NOT set here: a global `* text=auto eol=lf`.
#
# Parts of this tree are already stored with CRLF — InstanceTree.jrag among
# them — so a blanket rule would mark thousands of untouched files as modified
# on the next checkout and bury real changes under renormalisation noise.
# Normalising the whole repository is worth doing, but it needs to be its own
# commit, made deliberately:
#
#     # after adding `* text=auto eol=lf` above
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "Normalise line endings to LF"
#
# and merged when no long-lived branch is waiting, since it conflicts with
# everything. Until then, the rules below cover the cases where the line ending
# is not cosmetic but load-bearing.

# --- Files that must keep CRLF in the working tree --------------------------
# cmd.exe misparses a batch file with bare LF line endings.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# --- Files that must keep LF even on Windows --------------------------------
# A shell script or a Makefile with CRLF fails at the shebang or the recipe.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
configure.ac    text eol=lf
Makefile*       text eol=lf
*.mk            text eol=lf
gradlew         text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf

# --- Binary: never touch, never diff ----------------------------------------
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
*.gz            binary
*.tgz           binary
*.bz2           binary
*.xz            binary
*.jar           binary
*.class         binary
*.so            binary
*.so.*          binary
*.dylib         binary
*.dll           binary
*.exe           binary
*.o             binary
*.a             binary
*.lib           binary
*.pyc           binary
*.pyd           binary
*.mat           binary
*.fmu           binary
*.fmux          binary

# --- Language hints ---------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub's language detection reports this repository as partly "Motoko" because
# .mo is Motoko's extension; here it is Modelica, which is most of the tree.
*.mo            linguist-language=Modelica
*.mop           linguist-language=Modelica

# Vendored and generated trees should not count towards language statistics and
# should be collapsed in pull request diffs by default.
ThirdParty/**       linguist-vendored
external/**         linguist-vendored
*.jrag              linguist-language=Java
*.jadd              linguist-language=Java
*.ast               linguist-language=Java

# --- Export ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep development-only files out of `git archive` tarballs.
/.github        export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/.gitignore     export-ignore
